.TH WTWM-CONFIG 1 "2026-08-18" "wtwm 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wtwm-config \- validate and inspect a wtwm/twm configuration file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wtwm-config
.I file
.br
.B wtwm-config
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wtwm-config
parses one file with the same portable configuration engine used by
.BR wtwm (1).
It prints the effective scalar settings, color blocks, match lists, bindings,
menus, functions, and compatibility classification counts.  It does not start
a Wayland compositor, execute configured commands, read the normal fallback
search path, or change the file.
.PP
Use this command before selecting a wtwm login session or after editing an
existing twm configuration:
.PP
.EX
wtwm-config "$HOME/.twmrc" >/tmp/wtwm-config.dump
.EE
.PP
The dump is intended for inspection and regression diagnosis.  Its labels may
grow as configuration support grows; it is not a stable scripting interface.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Syntax and input errors are written to standard error with the source filename
and line number when available.  Recognized compatibility directives that do
not affect compositor state are accepted and counted in the output rather than
silently reinterpreted as another feature.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The file parsed successfully, or help was requested.
.TP
.B 1
The file could not be read or parsed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH SECURITY
Parsing does not run
.B f.exec
commands, functions, menu entries, or startup commands.  A successful parse does
not make commands in an imported file trustworthy; review them before starting
wtwm.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wtwm (1),
.BR wtwmrc (5),
.BR twm (1)
